4. Rearrange the order of widgets inside your ColumnIn this task, rearrange the widgets inside the `Column` so 
that the **ElevatedButton appears at the top**, followed by the two `Text` widgets.

Code:
dart
body: Center(
  child: Column(
    mainAxisSize: MainAxisSize.min,
    children: [
      ElevatedButton(
        onPressed: () {
          setState(() {
            food = "Updated!";
          });
        },
        child: const Text("Update"),
      ),

      const SizedBox(height: 20),

      Text(
        food,
        style: const TextStyle(
          fontSize: 22,
          fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,
        ),
      ),

      const SizedBox(height: 20),

      const Text(
        "My Favorite IPL Team: Chennai Super Kings",
        style: TextStyle(
          fontSize: 22,
          fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,
        ),
      ),
    ],
  ),
)

UI Order:

Before:

1. Favorite Food Text
2. Favorite IPL Team Text
3. Button

After rearranging:

1. Update Button
2. Favorite Food Text
3. Favorite IPL Team Text

How the UI changes:

When the app is run, the **Update button moves to the top** of the screen. 
The favorite food text appears below the button, and the favorite IPL team text appears below the food text.

This happens because a `Column` displays its `children` **from top to bottom in the same order in which they are written in the code.
